{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/406469-putting-the-seelie-and-unseelie-courts-in-lost","id":406469,"title":"Putting the Seelie and Unseelie Courts in Lost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-15T00:35:04-08:00","id":406469,"title":"Putting the Seelie and Unseelie Courts in Lost","content":"As we all know, a recognizable staple of faerie lore are the Seelie and Unseelie Courts. Hell, they are prominent in Dreaming as the two sides of a Game of Thrones-like plot. I wonder how can the Seelie and Unseelie Courts be represented in Lost? Since these Courts deal with beauty and the vainness that comes with it, would the Seelie harvest Vanity as its emotion and Jealousy for the Unseelie? What Contracts would be tied to these Courts? How would they repel the Gentry?<br /> <br /> Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T01:12:16-08:00","id":406496,"title":"","content":"As of the current edition, the &quot;Seelie&quot; and &quot;Unseelie&quot; Courts are specifically the Scottish alliance of the Spring &amp; Summer Courts and of the Autumn &amp; Winter Courts.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of opposed Courts that harvest Vanity and Jealousy though! The only problem is the juxtaposition of feeling it and inspiring it. Because I know you're going for the Seelie Court being Vain beauties/nobles, and the Unseelie Court being grasping usurpers - but inspiring vanity (which you'd have to do to feed off of it) means fanning the flames of someone's ego, which is less the theme your going for. If anything, being the transcedant vain beauty inspires jealousy, not vanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T01:30:13-08:00","id":406501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/406469-putting-the-seelie-and-unseelie-courts-in-lost?p=406496#post406496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of the current edition, the &quot;Seelie&quot; and &quot;Unseelie&quot; Courts are specifically the Scottish alliance of the Spring &amp; Summer Courts and of the Autumn &amp; Winter Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I like this, as those have sense inside a setting, and make nice alliance for Courts to fight with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T02:17:41-08:00","id":406528,"title":"","content":"I did like the idea of a different alliance model in New Orleans, where the Rada Court was formed by Winter and Spring Changelings (Sorrow &amp; Desire), and the Petwo Court was formed by Summer and Autumn Changelings (Wrath &amp; Fear). The Rada Court holds dominance from the Winter Solstice till the Summer Solstice (the period of time during which days grow progressively longer), the Petwo Court holds dominance from the Summer Solstice to the Winter Solstice (the period of time during which the days grow progressively shorter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T02:27:35-08:00","id":406530,"title":"","content":"The Sun and Moon Courts make more sense as Seelie and Unseelie than anything Slavic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T03:14:56-08:00","id":406547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/406469-putting-the-seelie-and-unseelie-courts-in-lost?p=406528#post406528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did like the idea of a different alliance model in New Orleans, where the Rada Court was formed by Winter and Spring Changelings (Sorrow &amp; Desire), and the Petwo Court was formed by Summer and Autumn Changelings (Wrath &amp; Fear). The Rada Court holds dominance from the Winter Solstice till the Summer Solstice (the period of time during which days grow progressively longer), the Petwo Court holds dominance from the Summer Solstice to the Winter Solstice (the period of time during which the days grow progressively shorter).</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool idea, would be very found of finding other possible Seasonal Alliances and their meaning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/406469-putting-the-seelie-and-unseelie-courts-in-lost?p=406530#post406530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sun and Moon Courts make more sense as Seelie and Unseelie than anything Slavic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Courts also have they problems - mainly, their whole &quot;we must fight with each other every day&quot;.<br /> \u200b<br /> It's from common misconception of anglosaxon researches that <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belobog\" target=\"_blank\">Belobog</a> and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chernobog\" target=\"_blank\">Chernobog</a> were opposing forces - in reality, they more looked like brothers, filing one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T03:44:40-08:00","id":406552,"title":"","content":"They don't fight which each other every day. They're actually a pretty good implementation of Belobog and Chernobog as brothers filling out each other.<br /> <br /> A healthy Durinal Freehold can be defined as &quot;Work hard all day, play hard all night&quot;. The Sun Court &quot;fight&quot; the Moon Court to impose limits on their uncontrolled and dangerous revelry. The Moon Court &quot;fight&quot; the Sun Court to impose limits on their uncontrolled authoritarian behaviour. Throguh &quot;fighting&quot; they achieve a healthy balance.<br /> <br /> I do think the presentation could have been a bit more explicit about it. And Disgust is a terrible emotion for partying all night; Joy would be much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T04:01:59-08:00","id":406558,"title":"","content":"Well actually if we're going to be realistic about ancient Slavic myths - there's no evidence Belobog was ever even a thing. He was more or less retroactively invented by later scholars out of the supposition that Chernobog as an &quot;evil&quot; Black God (at least as he was characterized by Christian monks in the 12th Century who recorded the rites), would have a &quot;good&quot; White God counterpart.<br /> <br /> There's no real evidence of dualism in pre-Christian Slavic belief systems at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}